Know that rituals are any set of noninstinctive predictable series of social actions that:
- cannot be justified by a rational means-to-ends explanation;
- are non-rational, mystical, non-utilitarian, sacred, and generate in the performers certain sentiments useful to society;
- are communicative, aesthetic and expressive;
- express power which can coerce and control the behaviour of others; and,
- are a dramatization of myth that can provide a model for correct moral attitudes in secular life.

